/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Archimedean.TruncatedIcosidodecahedron.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 48`, `matAt x 39` and `(x 57, x 58)` are a weak fit of `Archimedean.TruncatedIcosidodecahedron.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem archimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Archimedean.TruncatedIcosidodecahedron.polyhedron Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.S N 48 39 57 := by
  rw [Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.len_eq Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.par_ok Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.zs_eq Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.weak_ok Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.poly_eq Pose.ArchimedeanTruncatedIcosidodecahedron.ok

end Nieuwland.Polyhedra
